	abstract = {Proposes a lexical access from spectra (LAFS) model that combines expected phonological and acoustic-phonetic properties of English word sequences into a simple spectral-sequence decoding network structure. Phonetic segments and phonological rules play an important role in network compilation, but not in the direct analysis of the speech waveform during lexical search. There is no feature-detector stage in LAFS. If viewed as a perceptual model, LAFS constitutes a simple null hypothesis against which to compare and refine alternative theories of acoustic analysis and lexical search. (4 p ref) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2017 APA, all rights reserved)},
